{"lines": ["Now check the sky that night.", "A skeptic, Joe Nickell, wrote in Skeptical Inquirer in the year 2000 that the bright object was most likely a meteor. It was seen across Maryland, Pennsylvania, and West Virginia the same evening.", "And the red pulsing light Nunley described? Nickell proposed it was three flashing red aircraft beacons.", "That is a proposal, not a proof. But one strange night becomes two ordinary lights, and each can be checked.", "As for the figure, Nickell suggested a startled barn owl on a branch, with the foliage behind it looking like a pleated skirt.", "The next day, a newspaperman, A. Lee Stewart Junior, reported skid marks and an odd, gummy deposit. A local boy, Max Lockard, later admitted he had driven his truck around the site, hoping to see something.", "Rule two. Count every light you can name before you count the ones you can't. Meteor, beacon, headlight. Then ask what is left."], "words": [["Now", 0.0, 0.16], ["check", 0.16, 0.36], ["the", 0.36, 0.52], ["sky", 0.52, 0.72], ["that", 0.72, 0.98], ["night.", 0.98, 1.22], ["A", 2.04, 2.12], ["skeptic,", 2.12, 2.62], ["Joe", 2.8, 2.96], ["Nickell,", 2.96, 3.36], ["wrote", 3.36, 3.7], ["in", 3.7, 3.98], ["Skeptical", 3.98, 4.32], ["Inquirer", 4.32, 5.4], ["in", 5.4, 5.5], ["the", 5.5, 5.6], ["year", 5.6, 5.76], ["2000", 5.76, 6.08], ["that", 6.08, 6.76], ["the", 6.76, 6.88], ["bright", 6.88, 7.12], ["object", 7.12, 7.52], ["was", 7.52, 7.96], ["most", 7.96, 8.18], ["likely", 8.18, 8.68], ["a", 8.68, 8.88], ["meteor.", 8.88, 9.12], ["It", 9.82, 9.92], ["was", 9.92, 10.04], ["seen", 10.04, 10.32], ["across", 10.32, 10.68], ["Maryland,", 10.68, 11.16], ["Pennsylvania,", 11.74, 12.1], ["and", 12.1, 12.74], ["West", 12.74, 12.96], ["Virginia", 12.96, 13.5], ["the", 13.5, 13.88], ["same", 13.88, 14.16], ["evening.", 14.16, 14.6], ["And", 15.42, 15.54], ["the", 15.54, 15.64], ["red", 15.64, 15.84], ["pulsing", 15.84, 16.4], ["light", 16.4, 16.6], ["Nunley", 16.6, 17.16], ["described?", 